abstract: >-
  A controlled, pre-registered study of why language-conditioned robot policies ignore their instructions.
  Visuomotor imitation policies are trained from scratch with data budget, expert, architecture and recipe
  held fixed; only the fraction f of contrastive scenes changes. Counterfactual instruction following rises
  from 48.9% at f = 0 to 71.3% at f = 0.5 with no loss in nominal success; small doses have no detectable
  effect; failures are hesitations rather than shortcuts; and with only four scenes the familiar VLA failure
  returns. The pre-registration is commit 39bf011 (tag prereg-39bf011).
